    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`). The request may now include an optional ISO `birthDate`; when present, the response returns `ageBand` as `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (65+), computed as full years against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` (read-only string enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and the `AgeBandEnum`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`birth_date`) `LocalDate` column with getter/setter, so the band can be recomputed at read time.\n- **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column; also padded the hsqldb positional seed inserts with the extra `NULL`.\n- **`AgeBand.java`** (new util) \u2014 derives `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` from `birthDate` vs `registrationDate` using `Period.between(...).getYears()`, returning `null` when no birth date was supplied.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `ageBand` via the util; `birthDate` maps by name automatically.\n\nThe new `Cp34Tests` (birthDate `1990-01-01`, registered 2026-08-21 \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and all 47 existing tests remain green.",
